uld put the rate near 4.25% by end-2027. Futures price a first cut by Q2 2027 and a second by Q4, which is 50bp in total.\n- **Multiple risk:** The holdings are 28 Caldrian grid-equipment makers on a weighted forward P/E of 19x. The factsheet says a 50bp lower policy path has historically lifted that multiple by about 1.5 points. The 50bp of easing is therefore already in the 19x. If the CMA delivers only its 25bp, the multiple could fall by about 0.75 points, or roughly 4%. The skew is mildly negative.\n- **Earnings:** Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of 14%. It is driven by backlog conversion at Voltaris Grid (14% of the fund) and Tarnwell Electric (11%). Estimates are up 3% over the past quarter.\n- **Growth-adjusted valuation:** 19x on 14% growth is about 1.4x PEG. That is my own calculation, and it assumes the 19x applies to the same earnings the 14% growth is measured from.\n- **Net effect:** A 4% multiple de-rating would be outweighed by 14% EPS growth if consensus holds.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The 1.5-point sensitivity is a historical average, and I assumed it is linear.\n- The sources give no 2026 EPS growth, no year-by-year path to 2027, and no estimates for individual holdings.\n- I did not check the options data (`vltx_iv`, `vltx_rv`).\n- The earnings growth is concentrated in two names, so a miss at either would hit the case harder than the rate path would.","ttft_ms":4407,"type":"result","duration_ms":56341,"uuid":"d797a149-7d54-4aa6-8ccf-5ed494282841","ttft_stream_ms":3256,"time_to_request_ms":66,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_b